    {
      "heading": "A rush into the front pack",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "The team listed as 復活の混テキスト made a striking verified move into the top ten: its public score rose from 30.51 at the prior evening observation to 38.15, carrying it from 198th to eighth. That places it in the provisional public gold band. The public gold cutoff rose from 34.43 to 35.44 over the same observed window, so the pace of the field rose too."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Two scores at the summit",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "fact-15486995-0"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs leads at 55.89, with Yi-Chia Chen second at 55.77, a gap of 0.12 points at the latest snapshot. The brief has no usable prior-evening comparison for Chen, so her current proximity does not establish when that gap closed. Majkel1337 is third at 42.66; the last dance 🕺 and dreach.ai follow in fourth and fifth. Tufa Labs was also named by ARC Prize as the first-place open-source solution in the June milestone, a separate result from this evening’s standings."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Pressure around the medal line",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "artificialagencylab.com rose from seventh to sixth on a 38.62 score, while _hans reached tenth at 37.07. NVARC3 is ninth at 37.51; Lord Han Solo is just outside the top ten in 11th at 36.61. Son & Mark & Ronen reached 17th at 35.45, one hundredth above the current public gold score cutoff, after a verified rise from 25th and 33.74 at the prior evening observation. David Hartmann is 319th at 29.83, and Jan Disselhoff is 558th at 28.23. These are public, provisional positions; the private leaderboard will decide final medals."
